<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 50,280 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 50,280 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 50,280 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 38,194 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				     Monday	October 13</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 4,865	 9,585</p>
<p>    Import cargo		45,415	28,609</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, three were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		  39,000	 Miremare	     14/10</p>
<p>Furnace oil	    42,000	 Probe Hawk	   15/10</p>
<p>Palm oil		 16,000	 Bunga Sepang	 15/10</p>
<p>High speed diesel    52,000	 Al-Maqwa	     16/10</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
